@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option Desk - Behavior tests and the unit coverage gate

component "Production packages\nengine / shell / agent" as code
component "Unit\nin-process, external boundaries replaced\nhappy and failure cases" as unit
component "BDD\nGherkin + synthetic command workflows\nhappy and failure scenarios" as bdd
component "Integration\nCLI / MCP processes, loopback HTTP\nChromium, installer checks" as integration
component "Validation\ndocs, packaging, evidence\nand coverage-gate checks" as validation
component "Unit line coverage\n80% minimum in EACH package\ncomplete production file denominator" as gate #C6E9C6
component "CI\nPython 3.11 and 3.13\nreports, refresh, mutation checks" as ci
code --> unit
code --> bdd
code --> integration
code --> validation
unit --> gate
gate --> ci
bdd --> ci
integration --> ci
validation --> ci
note bottom of gate
BDD and integration coverage do not enter this measurement.
Branch coverage is recorded without a separate minimum.
A passing total cannot offset an under-covered package.
end note
note bottom of unit
TDD is a sequence: observe the intended failure,
implement the behavior, then observe the same test pass.
It is not a fifth test layer.
end note

caption Sources: conftest.py, .coveragerc, scripts/check_unit_coverage.py and .github/workflows/refresh.yml.
@enduml
